  "worked_solution": "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}-3t \\\\ {t}^{2}+t+1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(0)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot {e}^{2(0)} \\\\ {e}^{2(0)}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot {0}^{2}-3\\cdot 0 \\\\ {0}^{2}+0+1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}+1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=-3 \\\\ {c}_{2}+1=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{1}=-3.$ From the second equation, we have ${c}_{2}=2.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=-3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}-3t \\\\ {t}^{2}+t+1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
